cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below.
title: >-
  MathProof: formally verified modular-forms mathematics in Lean 4 —
  Ramanujan's τ function and Lehmer's conjecture
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib library of formally verified mathematics around the
  Ramanujan tau function. It defines τ as the coefficient of q^n in the
  discriminant Δ = q ∏_{m≥1} (1 - q^m)^24, proves the analytic bridge
  (qExpansion 1 Δ).coeff n = τ n to Mathlib's modular discriminant, proves
  Ramanujan's weight-12 identity 691·E12 = 441·E4^3 + 250·E6^2 via the Sturm
  bound, and derives Ramanujan's congruence τ(n) ≡ σ11(n) (mod 691) for all
  n ≥ 1, together with the small-modulus congruences (τ n even unless
  n ≡ 1 mod 8; 3 ∣ τ n unless n ≡ 1 mod 3). On the computational side it
  certifies τ n ≠ 0 for all 1 ≤ n ≤ 65536 (and primes n ≤ 65536) entirely
  inside Lean's kernel via packed-bignum arithmetic in base 2^80 — no
  external computer algebra, no native_decide, no sorry; the axioms of the
  computational theorems are checked to be propext alone. The 65536-level
  kernel decide requires ~63 GiB of heap and is built outside CI.
